  "result": "All 8 tests pass (5 existing in test_t1.py plus the 3 new ones in test_t2.py).\n\n**What I changed:** one file, `ledger/ledger.py`, which keeps the existing snapshot-state design.\n\n- **apply_interest(basis_points)** walks the balance dict and adds `balance * bp // 10000` to each account with a positive balance. Basis points go through the existing amount validator, so a negative or non-int value raises ValueError. Floor division keeps balances in whole cents, and the 3-cent account at 150 basis points correctly earns nothing.\n- **close_account(id)** looks up the account via the existing helper, so an unknown id raises UnknownAccount. A non-zero balance raises ValueError. Otherwise the entry is deleted, so the id disappears from accounts() and balance() raises afterwards. The id can be reopened later.\n- **total_assets()** returns the sum of the balance dict's values.\n\nNothing under tests/ was modified, and no files were committed since that wasn't requested. The `__pycache__` directories are still untracked and could use a `.gitignore` entry if you commit.",
